cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite the companion paper (preferred-citation below)."
title: "How leaky is your inference API? Detecting model weight steganographic exfiltration"
abstract: >-
  A write-up and interactive demo of a covert channel in an LLM inference API:
  a compromised server hides model-weight bits in which tokens it emits, and a
  colluding client decodes them from the returned logprobs. Inference
  verification with an anytime-valid (e-process) aggregate detector catches it.
